# Ownership is the last line of defence when a change is textually innocuous but
# semantically a policy change. Pinning a feature by digest, widening a CVE
# threshold, or moving a tool version in tools.lock all look like routine edits
# and are all trust decisions.
#
# NOTE: two teams on one line means EITHER may approve, not both. GitHub has no
# "one approval from each team" primitive. Genuine dual control comes from
# Required Reviewers on the Review-Actor and Release-Actor environments, not
# from this file.
#
# All three teams must exist and have repository access, or CODEOWNERS matches
# nothing and "require review from Code Owners" becomes a silent no-op. Verify:
#   gh api orgs/infrashift/teams/<slug> --jq .slug

*                                   @infrashift/platform-engineers

# --- Trust decisions -------------------------------------------------------
# The policy that decides whether a release may proceed, and the keys used to
# verify the evidence it decides on.
/.github/pdp/                       @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/policies.rego          @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/policies_test.rego     @infrashift/security-admins
/.github/pdp/public-keys/           @infrashift/security-admins

# Tool versions and their checksums. These binaries run in the job that holds
# the signing key, so a version bump here is a supply-chain decision.
/tools.lock                         @infrashift/security-admins @infrashift/devops-leads
/scripts/install-tools.sh           @infrashift/security-admins @infrashift/devops-leads

# --- Pipeline engines ------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/                 @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins
/scripts/                           @infrashift/devops-leads

# --- What ships inside a template ------------------------------------------
# The shared Containerfile is copied into every template, so one edit changes
# all five published images.
/shared/                            @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins
# Feature references and their pins decide what code runs in a developer's
# container.
/src/                               @infrashift/devops-leads @infrashift/security-admins

# --- Repository security posture -------------------------------------------
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @infrashift/security-admins
/.gitleaks.toml                     @infrashift/security-admins
/.gitignore                         @infrashift/security-admins
/SETUP-ENVIRONMENTS.md              @infrashift/security-admins

# --- Documentation ---------------------------------------------------------
/docs/                              @infrashift/platform-engineers
/README.md                          @infrashift/platform-engineers
/TODO.md                            @infrashift/platform-engineers
